&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, you will lead an engineering team to ensure fast, high-quality execution. You will focus on rapid experimentation and technical excellence across the full customer lifecycle - from awareness and acquisition through to retention, revenue, and referral.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Operating at the intersection of engineering, product, and growth marketing, you will partner with cross-functional stakeholders to translate strategic visions into scalable engineering solutions. You will be responsible for empowering your team, optimising execution velocity, and maintaining high engineering standards as we scale our preventative care ecosystem globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ensure High-Quality Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Manage an engineering team or function to drive fast, reliable software delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve Technical &amp;amp; Operational Blockers:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as an escalation point for complex technical and operational issues, solving them efficiently to keep projects on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimise Workloads:&lt;/strong&gt; Balance priorities and take active responsibility for optimising team workload to maintain predictable delivery without burnout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Growth &amp;amp; Experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the execution of sophisticated, data-driven experiments and growth initiatives across the entire patient journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve Engineering Processes:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously refine development processes, workflows, and team structures to build a high-velocity environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build &amp;amp; Mentor Talent:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with talent acquisition teams to recruit, onboard, and retain world-class engineers while fostering a culture of ownership, psychological safety, and high morale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align Cross-Functionally&lt;/strong&gt; : Partner seamlessly with Product, Marketing, and Data stakeholders to align technical delivery with commercial goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Strength &amp;amp; Codebase Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; You are technically strong and partner credibly with senior engineers-able to evaluate system architecture and spot when technical estimates lack substance. Coding is not the primary job, but you are comfortable getting on the tools in an ecosystem built on React, React Native, TypeScript, Go microservices, GraphQL, Kubernetes, and GCP, and delivering work to unblock your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record managing an engineering team to ensure fast and high-quality execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Focus:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated capability in solving escalated issues, optimising team workloads, and driving continuous improvements across team workflows and structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation &amp;amp; Growth Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on background or strong familiarity with rapid experimentation, A/B testing, and building software optimised for user engagement, conversion, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People-First Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at mentoring engineers, navigating shifting priorities, and nurturing an inclusive, highly motivated team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional communication skills with a history of bridging technical delivery with product strategy, growth marketing, and commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in regulated sectors (such as healthtech, fintech or gaming), finding creative paths forward inside compliance constraints rather than being stopped by them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why join Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s next&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Our goal for the next three years is to support 1 million patients globally to live better for longer, launching into new conditions, demographics and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build something world-changing&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- We&#39;re on the path to becoming the world&#39;s largest international digital healthcare company. It will be challenging, fast-paced and deeply rewarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make real impact&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Your work directly shapes patient outcomes and scales evidence-based care across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate your growth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- High ownership, continuous feedback and dedicated development support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a motivated team&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Talented peers solving complex clinical and operational problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What&#39;s ahead in the UK&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be an owner&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Your own stake in the business with our employee options programme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Invest in your growth&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Annual development budget plus 3 days of professional development leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work flexibly&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Hybrid setup with 3 days a week in our Old Street office, designed for focus and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your well-being&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- Private health insurance through Vitality, or a monthly wellness allowance to spend on what matters most to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take time off&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- 25 days of holiday, enhanced parental leave and work from anywhere 3 weeks a year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join a connected team&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;- A vibrant office culture with regular socials, clubs, after-school sport and seasonal events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Eucalyptus&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re on a mission to make good health last a lifetime. More than 1 billion people live with obesity worldwide, driving preventable chronic conditions. We&#39;re here to build better long-term care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is now part of Hims &amp;amp; Hers, the global leader in personalised health and wellness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Euc is the company behind Juniper, one of the world&#39;s largest weight-management programs combining GLP-1 medication with personalised nutrition, movement support, and clinician-led care from prescribers, nurses, health coaches, pharmacists, and dietitians. Our published clinical research shows that our combined clinical and behavioural approach helps patients lose significantly more weight during their treatment with Juniper by four times.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Our Growth Story:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting patients living with obesity across our 5 markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Received selective NICE endorsement to provide services to the NHS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailored our offering to thousands of patients in Australia, the UK, Germany, Japan and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Eucalyptus is building one of the world’s largest international digital healthcare companies. As we scale across brands, markets and care models, patient operations needs to grow without losing quality, safety or trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director, International Patient Operations, you’ll lead the operating model behind patient care across eight brand-markets, our Manila hub, workforce planning, AI-enabled support, patient insights and partner operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior commercial operations role, not a traditional support leadership role. You’ll work where patient experience, clinical risk, market growth, automation, partner economics and service delivery meet. You’ll decide where capacity goes, where automation should and shouldn’t be used, which problems need product or clinical intervention, and what trade-offs we make across markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner closely with market GMs, Clinical, Product, Growth, Finance, Workforce Planning, AI and operational teams. You’ll have around seven direct reports and report to our Chief Commercial Officer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re open to this as a twelve-month fixed term or permanent hire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead global patient operations across markets.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the performance rhythm across market teams, Manila, workforce planning, AI-enabled support and partner operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make resolution the measure.&lt;/strong&gt; Improve complete resolution, reopens, quality, response times, AI containment and 24-hour care, with patient safety and clinical escalation risk visible throughout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Turn patient insight into action.&lt;/strong&gt; Use contact drivers, unresolved reasons, complaints, reopens, escalations and verbatims to identify where the journey is breaking and influence Product, Clinical, Growth, automation and market operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make commercial service trade-offs.&lt;/strong&gt; Balance cost to serve, service quality, clinical risk, growth and capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow the function’s commercial contribution.&lt;/strong&gt; Own proactive outreach, cancellation saves, payment recovery and conversion alongside cost to serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape the global capacity model.&lt;/strong&gt; Decide market by market where capacity should sit, how it should flex, and how we avoid solving every growth problem with more headcount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decide what varies by market and what stays the same.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the standard for what should feel like one company, and what needs to differ because of language, regulation or clinical risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the channel question.&lt;/strong&gt; Decide when channels like live chat, WhatsApp and voice earn their place, and when they dilute focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead through growth and integration.&lt;/strong&gt; Support new brand, market and operating-model integrations while protecting core service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build market leads who decide for themselves.&lt;/strong&gt; Coach leaders to reason through automation, headcount and channel trade-offs without escalating every call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create decision-quality reporting.&lt;/strong&gt; Build a monthly rhythm that helps GMs and senior leaders understand performance, root causes, trade-offs and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take command when priorities collide.&lt;/strong&gt; Bring structure, judgement and pace when launches, backlogs, clinical escalations, partner constraints or capacity conflicts compete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What good looks like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In your first year:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patients are getting faster, safer and more complete resolution across our largest markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market teams, Manila, workforce planning, AI and partner operations are working to one clear operating rhythm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Patient insight is informing product, clinical, automation and market decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GMs have a clear monthly view of performance, root causes, trade-offs and actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth, launches and integrations are supported without destabilising core service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are improving cost to serve without hiding patient risk or relying on team heroics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The function’s commercial contribution has grown through saves, payment recovery and proactive outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Market leads are making more automation, headcount and channel calls themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a senior operations leader who has run complex, high-volume service environments where the stakes were real. You may come from healthcare, digital health, financial services, insurance, consumer subscription, marketplace, BPO/vendor operations or another regulated or consequence-heavy setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand the commercial mechanics of service: demand, capacity, productivity, quality, cost to serve, cost per resolution, partner economics and automation. You can use data to make decisions, and you know when the numbers are incomplete and judgement is required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are likely to have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led a patient-facing or customer-facing operation at meaningful scale, ideally around &lt;strong&gt;200+ people&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;150+ plus a partner network&lt;/strong&gt; whose performance and commercials you owned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operated across multiple markets, countries or customer segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked deeply with offshore, captive or BPO capacity, including SLAs, rate cards, ramps, QBRs, partner performance and site economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Made trade-offs between service levels, cost, growth, risk and customer or patient outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Used patient or customer insight to influence decisions beyond your own function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked in an environment where quality, compliance, safety or trust genuinely mattered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operated across languages and different regulatory regimes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Moved work between locations and handled the team and commercial impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presented recommendations to senior leaders and influenced decisions with clear written work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be a strong fit if you:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can separate signal from noise in messy operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think commercially without losing sight of the patient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are confident challenging market asks, vendor claims and product trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know when automation improves the journey and when it moves risk elsewhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can write a clear one-page recommendation with options, trade-offs and a defensible number.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay calm when priorities conflict and decisions have to be made quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build teams and operating systems that reduce dependence on individual heroics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get more satisfaction from a market lead making a good call without you than from making it yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energised by a role whose scope changes as the business does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus points&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built or scaled a multi-market service operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve launched a new market, site, hub or support function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve integrated an acquired team, brand or operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve moved a high-volume support operation onto AI or automation while protecting quality and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve made a captive-versus-vendor decision and can explain the maths behind it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built strong successors or promoted people into your former scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve grown a revenue or retention line from inside a service function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Eucalyptus, we value individuals from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and we embrace the unique qualities each person brings. When you apply, please let us know of any reasonable adjustments you may need during the interview process. We use AI-assisted tools across our business to help our teams work more efficiently, including within our recruitment process. These tools support our team — all hiring decisions are made by real people, and every application is reviewed by a member of our recruitment team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOUT TIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we help SMEs save time and money in the running of their businesses by not only offering business accounts and related banking services, but also a comprehensive set of highly usable and connected administrative solutions, from invoicing to accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tide is transforming the small business banking market and now supports over 2 million members globally across the UK, India, Germany and France.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using advanced technology, all solutions are designed with SMEs in mind. With quick onboarding, low fees and innovative features, we thrive on making data driven decisions to serve our mission: to help SMEs save time and money so they can get back to doing what they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tide facts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tide is available for UK, Indian, German and French SMEs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2 million members across UK and India&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over $300 million raised in funding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Over 2,800 Tideans globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognised with Great Place to Work certification three years in a row, and among India’s Top 50 Best Workplaces in Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance in 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have offices in Central London, with a member support and technology centre in Sofia, Bulgaria, technology centres in Serbia, Romania, Lithuania and Hyderabad and offices in Gurugram, New Delhi, Berlin, Paris and Luxembourg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Reporting &amp;amp; Control team is responsible for the preparation of Tide’s key financial reports, as well as implementing and monitoring controls to safeguard the Group’s financial integrity.&amp;nbsp; The team plays a critical role in ensuring the financial data is accurate and complete, compliant with regulations and presented clearly to internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our Senior Financial Controller you’ll report to the Lead Financial Controller and be responsible for our credit products and areas of credit risk at Tide.&amp;nbsp; It’s exciting times here at Tide, we are scaling and developing our product offering at a phenomenal rate!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Financial Controller you will&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controllership of our proprietary credit offerings over our 3 Tide Capital companies with varying credit products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of the month end processes for reporting P&amp;amp;L, balance sheet and cashflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documenting and reviewing loss provisioning policies for credit risk, fraud and disputes, negative balances and other risk costs.&amp;nbsp; Ongoing monitoring and reporting of credit risk performance and adequacy of provisioning coefficients and methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring strong control of the new APPF fraud legislation, including accurate representation of losses from fraudulent transactions in the P&amp;amp;L and ensuring monthly balance sheet substantiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring strong control over our members accounts with negative (overdrawn) account balances, accurately reporting our P&amp;amp;L each month and ensuring monthly balance sheet substantiation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the Tide Credit Services business, product and operations teams to understand the performance of our products and ensure that our transactions are correctly recorded&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handling the introduction of new credit lending products along with our new investment product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the collections team for overdue loan payments, analyzing performance of recovery efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with the ongoing monitoring, operations and risk teams to monitor and report cost of risk, resulting from the credit portfolio, negative customer account balances, fraud and disputes, chargebacks, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working closely with the FP&amp;amp;A team to support with analysis, budgeting and forecasting of the credit portfolio and cost of risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the finance team at the Credit Risk Working Group and Risk and Compliance Committee.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building robust financial control processes and strengthening internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong balance sheet controls with monthly substantiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintaining relationships with external auditors, tax advisors and accounting advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collating financial data for the preparation of corporation tax ensuring compliance with tax legislation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifying opportunities to streamline and improve accounting processes, operations and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE ARE LOOKING FOR:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services – preferably in technology-driven &amp;amp; scale-up environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with credit products and provisioning for credit risk essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial acumen and excellent technical accounting skills. Familiar with accounting standard and disclosure requirements under UK GAAP and/or IFRS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dealt with the statutory audit of financial services company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold a professional finance qualification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive work with minimal hands-on management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort in taking responsibility for business-critical financial operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by Tide’s values and mission&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL GET IN RETURN:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Compensation -&amp;nbsp; competitive salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time Off – Generous annual leave on top of bank holidays.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Parental Leave – Paid maternity, paternity, and adoption leave to support your family journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sabbatical – Extended unpaid and paid leave options after completing milestone years with Tide&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to salary sacrifice benefits – like Nursery (could save up to 47% on fees!) and Cycle to Work discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health Insurance – Comprehensive Private family insurance plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life &amp;amp; Accident Cover – Comprehensive accidental and life insurance protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental Wellbeing – Access to therapy sessions, courses, meditations, and workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retirement Planning – Build your retirement fund faster with Tide’s pension scheme on eligible earnings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteering &amp;amp; Development Days – Paid days annually for volunteering or personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development – Annual budget for books, courses, coaching, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;WOO (Work Outside the Office) – Work from abroad for up to 90 days annually&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Setup – Contribution towards setting up your home office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Laptop Ownership – Keep your old laptop and get a new one when it’s time for a replacement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snacks &amp;amp; Meals – Daily&amp;nbsp;breakfast spread with all-day coffee, tea, and juices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TIDEAN WAYS OF WORKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we champion a &lt;strong&gt;flexible workplace &lt;/strong&gt;model that&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;supports both in-person and remote work to cater to the specific needs of our different teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While remote work is supported, we believe in the power of face-to-face interactions to foster team spirit and collaboration. Our offices are designed as hubs for innovation and team-building, where we encourage regular in-person gatherings to foster a strong sense of community.&lt;strong&gt; For this role we would expect the role holder to attend our Old Street offices at least one day a week. &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;TIDE IS A PLACE FOR EVERYONE&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tide, we believe that we can only succeed if we let our differences enrich our culture. Our Tideans come from a variety of backgrounds and experience levels. We consider everyone irrespective of their ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, family or parental status, national origin, veteran, neurodiversity or differently-abled status. We celebrate diversity in our workforce as a cornerstone of our success. Our commitment to a broad spectrum of ideas and backgrounds is what enables us to build products that resonate with our members’ diverse needs and lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are One Team and foster a transparent and inclusive environment, where everyone’s voice is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Tide, we thrive on diversity, embracing various backgrounds and experiences. We welcome all individuals regardless of ethnicity, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability. Our inclusive culture is key to our success, helping us build products that meet our members&#39; diverse needs. We are One Team, committed to transparency and ensuring everyone’s voice is heard.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
